This repository contains source code and project assets for Gravity Shift.
The code and content are provided for personal use, research, learning,
modding preparation, and limited development within the project scope.

This project is not distributed under a fully open-source license.
The author retains ownership over the base game, engine, runtime system,
and all content that forms the original Gravity Shift experience.


1. PERMITTED USE                                                      

You may:

- Install and run the game locally for personal gameplay.
- Study the source code and project structure for educational purposes.
- Create your own world/module folders, including files named with the
  suffix `_world` and their supporting resources, such as `main.py`,
  `objects.json`, and `Resources/` assets.
- Extend your own world logic using the original engine modules as support
  libraries at runtime, provided that your additions remain within your own
  world scope and do not replace or redistribute the engine as a standalone
  product.


2. RESTRICTED CORE                                                    

The following are considered protected core project materials and may not be
modified, copied, redistributed, or repackaged as part of a separate product:

- `core_v#/` directory and its contents;
- `START_HERE.py` and the main launch/navigation structure;
- the original runtime architecture, game engine classes, rendering logic,
  lighting system, save/load structure, and base gameplay logic;
- any files that define the original Gravity Shift engine behaviour.

Editing, changing, replacing, or redistributing these core files is not
permitted unless the author provides explicit written permission.


3. USER MODDING RIGHTS                                                

You may create and maintain your own `_world` content, including custom logic,
resource folders, object definitions, and gameplay configuration.

Within that scope, you may:

- write your own `main.py` logic;
- define your own `objects.json` data;
- add your own resources to `Resources/` folders;
- make your own world-specific combinations using the existing engine modules
  as part of the game runtime.

The author retains ownership of the original project and engine. Your custom
world is your authored modification, while the original Gravity Shift code
remains protected.


4. REDISTRIBUTION                                                     

You may not redistribute or publish the original engine/core files as a
standalone software package, project, or derivative game.

You may share your own `_world` additions only as a mod or extension that is
intended to be used together with Gravity Shift, and only if you clearly state
that the modification is your own work and that it relies on the original
project as a supporting game environment.


5. NO WARRANTY                                                        

The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability,
fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement.


6. COPYRIGHT NOTICE                                                   

Copyright notice and this license text must remain present in the project
where applicable.


7. FUTURE AUTHORIAL CONTROL                                           

This license is a custom source-available authorization model. The author
may revise, clarify, add, or remove permissions for particular project areas
at any time in future releases.

For the use of protected core areas, or for any licensing exceptions,
contact the author directly.


